#+TITLE: Windows installed-prefix verification truncates native stderr paths
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: ci
#+DEPENDS: native-windows-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/fermeture-cao-20261023
#+DATE: 2026-11-02

* Evidence
GitLab job17671615240 reports six prefix failures, although both runtime assets
are staged successfully. Windows PowerShell converts native stderr to error
records; Out-String's default width wraps paths containing spaces before the
prefix parser sees them. Each of three installations loses the two paths.

* Correction under qualification
Capture the diagnostic with Out-String -Width32767 in both invocations.
A real Windows fake-executable fixture reproduces truncation at width80 and
preserves the complete source path with the explicit width. Native installed
and moved-prefix CI must still pass before this issue can be closed.

* Resolved -- 2026-11-02
Windows job17671893337 (pipeline3018736618) passes the full installed, bare
launcher, moved-prefix and explicit-override checks with the correction.
The source script is identical in the two CAD qualification branches.
